## Activity Timeline Implementation — Full Analysis

### 1. Data Layer: How `activity_timeline` Is Built

**File:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/session.ts`

#### Types

```typescript
// Line 221-228 — CommitSummary (git commit with parsed trailer refs)
export interface CommitSummary {
  hash: string;        // 7-char short hash
  full_hash: string;
  date: string;        // ISO string
  message: string;
  author: string;
  task_refs: string[]; // slugs parsed from "Task: @slug" trailers in commit body
}

// Line 212-219 — CompletedTaskSummary
export interface CompletedTaskSummary {
  ref: string;                   // short ULID (8 chars)
  slug: string | null;
  title: string;
  completed_at: string;
  closed_reason: string | null;
  origin?: "manual" | "derived" | "observation_promotion";
}

// Line 235-243 — ActivityItem (the union type)
export type ActivityItem =
  | { type: "task_completion"; date: string; task: CompletedTaskSummary }
  | { type: "commit"; date: string; commit: CommitSummary }
  | {
      type: "linked_commit";
      date: string;
      commit: CommitSummary;
      task: CompletedTaskSummary;
    };
```

#### Trailer Parsing in Git Layer

**File:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/utils/git.ts`, line 107:

```typescript
const trailerPattern = /^Task:\s*@([\w-]+)/gm;
```
Commits with `Task: @slug` in their body have the slug(s) extracted into `taskRefs: string[]`.

#### `buildActivityTimeline()` Function (lines 512-584)

```typescript
function buildActivityTimeline(
  completedTasks: CompletedTaskSummary[],
  commits: CommitSummary[],
  taskRefResolver: Map<string, string>,  // slug/ULID → short ULID ref
): ActivityItem[]
```

Logic:
1. Iterates all commits. If a commit has `task_refs`, it tries to resolve each ref via `taskRefResolver` (which maps slugs and ULIDs to the completed task's short ULID). If a completed task is found → emits a `linked_commit` entry using `max(commit.date, task.completed_at)` as the sort date, and marks the task as "linked" to prevent duplication.
2. If a commit has trailer refs but none resolve to a completed task, it's emitted as a plain `commit`.
